# draft
// SECOND DRAFT (M5): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
The gate of the slain is a table. You had pictured something grander.
It stands on a shelf of grey rock above the battlefield, long enough to seat forty, with one stool behind it and one stamp on it. Mist comes up from below and never quite clears. Beyond the mist, the dead are already queuing.
A tall woman in scale mail sits on the end of the table, eating an apple.
"You're the new one. I'm Skögul." # speaker: skogul
She looks at your hands, then your boots, then the queue.
"They'll all tell you they died well. Some of them did. Odin wants the ones who did." # speaker: skogul
She taps the stamp. It is heavier than it looks, and it has two faces.
"Weapon in hand when they fell: Valhalla. Anything else: Hel. That's the whole of the law this morning. It gets longer." # speaker: skogul
"Every soul you judge rightly is a ring in your purse. Every one you get wrong goes on the quartermaster's slate. He forgives two a day. After that he fines you, and he enjoys it." # speaker: skogul
You think of the roof at home, and of what a ring buys in winter.
* ["What if they lie?"]
  "They will. The dead talk. Bodies don't." # speaker: skogul
  "Look at the hands before you listen to the mouth. When a story and a body disagree, hold them side by side with the brass pin, and you've caught a liar. That's worth a ring of its own." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: flag asked_about_lies
* ["What if I'm wrong?"]
  "Then a braggart drinks with heroes, an honest farmer goes down to Hel, and neither of them thanks you." # speaker: skogul
  "Nobody is right every time. Be right more often than the quartermaster expects." # speaker: skogul
* [Pick up the stamp.]
  She watches you weigh it in your hand, and almost smiles.
  "Good. Odin likes the ones who don't ask." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: standing odin +1
- Skögul throws the apple core over the edge. It falls for a long time.
"The sun's up. When it sets, the gate closes. Don't dawdle." # speaker: skogul
The first of the dead shuffles out of the mist, holding his own helmet in both hands like a man come to ask a favour.
-> END
